From c0df126dc052ad29b558d8ac2574f64c84cfc6de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PathOps <noreply@pathops.dev>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 09:33:14 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] auth: enforce PathOps delegated authorization_details on
 the API

Tokens of the configured PathOps delegation issuer
([authorized_integration] PATHOPS_DELEGATION_ISSUER) are tokens the PathOps
Tenant Control Plane derived from one operation a user approved (PathOps
Decision 0050). Their Authorized Integration needs a broad scope (personal
repositories need write:user and write:repository), so the scope is not
the boundary; their RAR authorization_details are:

- such a token is accepted only when its integration pins sub and azp with
  equality rules, its azp is PATHOPS_DELEGATION_AUTHORIZED_PARTY, and the
  request is an API v1 request (never web, git, LFS or packages);
- its authorization_details must parse as the PathOps forgejo vocabulary
  (pathops_repository create/seed, pathops_webhook configure);
- every API request is then allowed only when a detail authorizes exactly
  its action on its owner/repository (and, for webhooks, its target URL and
  events); anything else gets 403 before a handler runs.

A token for gaston/app-a cannot create, read or change gaston/app-b, a
repository token cannot touch webhooks and a webhook token cannot create or
delete repositories. Without the setting, behavior is unchanged.
